From: Halcyon Linux <cports@halcyon-linux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] link the standalone libunwind

Chimera's standalone libunwind installs its shared object as
libunwind-nongnu.so, while LLVM's libunwind is the one that provides
libunwind.so. The bcachefs stack unwinder needs the former.

--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
     println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=udev");
     println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=keyutils");
     println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=aio");
-    println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=unwind");
+    println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=unwind-nongnu");
 
     // Export static symbols for dladdr() in tools-side prt_addr_symbol
     println!("cargo:rustc-link-arg-bins=-rdynamic");
